⚡⚡🇧🇷🇮🇱🇺🇸 Flávio Bolsonaro's escape from Brazil reportedly involved a former Israeli Mossad agent, two vans, an Argentine private jet and an internationally coordinated operation planned before his electoral defeat, according to an exclusive CNN Brasil investigation based on security footage and information obtained from Brazilian authorities.

The former Mossad operative, an Israeli-born naturalized American, reportedly arrived in Brazil on October 19 and personally accompanied Bolsonaro across the Argentine border on October 27. Bolsonaro and his family then boarded a Gulfstream G400 operated by Argentina's Baires Fly, stopping in Ecuador before reaching Miami. Investigators are examining reported assistance from officials linked to Javier Milei's government and US political figures. Brazilian government sources describe the operation, reportedly codenamed “Operation Alba,” as a planned international exfiltration rather than a spontaneous departure.

